SUMMARY:Aga Khan Program Fall 2026 An Evening With Lecture Series: Anna Pro
 nina: The “waqf question” in Soviet Turkestan and Architectural Restor
 ation
LOCATION:MIT\, 33 MASSACHUSETTS AVE\, Cambridge\, MA 02139
DESCRIPTION:Photo: Ernst Cohn-Wiener\, Photo of the Madrasah-i Ulugh Beg in
  Samarkand\, 1924-25 Source: The British museum In the early Soviet period
 \, the preservation of Islamic architecture in Central Asia became entangl
 ed with a struggle over the property and revenues that had historically su
 stained it. This talk examines the relationship between Islamic charitable
  endowments and Soviet preservation agencies in Samarkand between 1922 and
  1927\, focusing on the activities of the Samarkand Commission for the Pre
 servation and Restoration of Monuments and its parent institution\, Turkom
 staris. Facing chronic shortages of funding\, Turkomstaris sought access t
 o waqf revenues traditionally used to support mosques\, madrasas\, and shr
 ines. Their claims brought them into conflict with the newly established S
 oviet waqf administration\, as well as local Muslim communities and custod
 ians of endowed property. These disputes raised fundamental questions abou
 t who controlled waqf resources\, who had authority over Islamic buildings
 \, and what constituted legitimate restoration. Drawing on archival record
 s\, administrative correspondence\, and local press\, the talk explores ho
 w preservationists\, Soviet officials\, and Muslim communities negotiated 
 competing claims to waqf and architectural heritage and what argumentative
  strategies they used.\nhttps://calendar.mit.edu/event/aga-khan-program-fa
 ll-2026-an-evening-with-lecture-series-anna-pronina-the-waqf-question-in-s
 oviet-turkestan-and-architectural-restoration\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https:
 //pushpin.city/boston/
URL:https://calendar.mit.edu/event/aga-khan-program-fall-2026-an-evening-wi
 th-lecture-series-anna-pronina-the-waqf-question-in-soviet-turkestan-and-a
 rchitectural-restoration
END:VEVENT
